WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.280
[Intro music]

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:06.360
Now how about the mathematics?

00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:08.020
Behind this idea.

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:13.580
Well, you may not understand all the symbols, but just to kind of see what it looks like.

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:16.280
We wrote down equations.

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:20.700
Physicists wrote down equations way back, 60s and 70s that were...

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:24.400
wonderfully accurate at describing

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:27.280
the forces of nature--the non-gravitational forces.

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:30.840
The electromagnetic force, the weak and strong nuclear forces.

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:34.320
We've also written down equations that describe the

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:39.239
particles of matter in which those forces act, like electrons, and neutrinos, and quarks.

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:41.820
The puzzling thing is this:

00:00:41.890 --> 00:00:47.300
those equations have built in a fantastic amount of symmetry.

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:52.739
What I mean by symmetry is, if in everyday life if you have a snowflake if you rotate that

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:59.100
snowflake in the right way, it looks the same even though you've rotated it, you've transformed it it has...symmetry.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:03.200
If you take a sphere, that's even more symmetric.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:07.860
As you rotate a sphere, regardless of what angle you rotate it through, it looks the same.

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:15.140
Similarly, the basic equations had a built-in symmetry much like that. If you mixed up the pieces of the equations

00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:17.660
somehow it all coalesced that the overall

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:21.200
mathematical form stayed the same.

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:28.040
The problem was, if you wanted to give mass to the matter particles, or even some of the force carrying particles...

00:01:28.450 --> 00:01:33.450
we knew how to do that mathematically, but the new mathematical term looks like this

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:35.940
It has a psi bar and a psi in it.

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:39.320
That term, if you brought that into the equations

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:47.580
Ruin the symmetry. Symmetry was shattered completely went away and without the symmetry the equations were actually inconsistent.

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:53.340
They didn't work any longer. So, the mathematical puzzle was to try to give mass to the particles

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:55.960
but not destroy the symmetry

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:57.560
the idea of

00:01:57.579 --> 00:02:05.398
Higgs and various others was introduce a new term. One that didn't quite look like a mass term at first sight. One that was completely

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:11.639
symmetric like the others. When you brought this new term into the equations, the equations maintain their beautiful symmetry.

00:02:12.099 --> 00:02:18.649
But notice that if that first factor in front of psi bar * psi--we call it phi--that symbol sitting in front.

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:22.300
If that is rewritten as say, m

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:24.589
Plus h where m is just a number

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:27.900
Then when you multiply that through look what happens

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:36.200
The m multiplied to psi bar and the psi looks like a mass term, and that m is the constant value of the field that's

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:38.620
permeating space. So that

00:02:38.660 --> 00:02:43.780
permeating field in this mathematical guise gives rise to the mass of

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:46.300
particles. That's how the

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:48.880
mathematical form of this idea works.

